{"parentUuid":"ede355a5-3981-4815-b159-d26ac31720a8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"0f0e2f8d-d651-4ec1-abd6-8e7584892f0f","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash — Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds athlete performance data pipelines (Football GPS, force plate). Family: wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo as of 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-forward player-coach near Iowa, ~$90K+ floor, ~mid-2027. Deeper context: `~/DEV/ContextVault` — read before career/personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python + R. **macOS since 2026-08-05**; Windows 11 box still ACTIVE (synced 9/9). Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB; no cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval. OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Wants to be challenged, not affirmed — push on vague or rehearsed reasoning (\\\"sharpened, not soothed\\\").\\n- Defers technical micro-decisions when convention exists — decide, state it, move on.\\n- Builds incrementally. Nothing that breaks mid-season.\\n- Authors own direction when leadership doesn't; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo org.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads\\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: `DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`, pushed 9/9. NEXT: real-phone check; host or keep local. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes.\\n- **Baseball profiles (9/2)**: `DEV/Baseball_PerformanceProfiles`, Excel-only coach. 3 .xlsx mock-data prototypes. NEXT: coach picks one + real tests.\\n- **RTP CLA course (9/10)**: ingest + PDF rebuild DONE. NEXT: import .ris → Zotero; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla-course.\\n- **ATH Tech framework (8/14)**: shipped. NEXT: Micah mtg (need ITS intake path); inventory refresh due 9/29. →Tier A ath-tech-framework, tech-inventory-refresh.\\n- **Kinexon volleyball (8/1)**: API email→CSM, awaiting docs. Plan: sync→SQLite→dashboards; CSV interim.\\n- **Status report (9/7)**: #2 drafted, UNSENT — `SecondBrain/Inbox/status-reports/2026-09-07-email.txt`. NEXT: read-check, send, rename `-email-sent.txt`, flip `sent: true`. #3 = 9/21. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline.\\n- **Acro & Tumbling (9/8)**: owe an Excel \\\"pass builder\\\" — routines → cumulative impact load. 5-athlete pilot. Awaiting skill inventory + assignments.\\n- **Open PRs (9/7)**: AgentAssist #1 (draft), CFB_Analytics_Lab #1. Deferred: FA26 camp regex.\\n- **OKR/JD 2026 (7/17)**: Blake LEFT, AJ owns FB. →vault `Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026/`.\\n- Parked in Tier A: Fireflies key rotation; child dental.\\n\\n- **Skill audit (9/12)**: DONE. 160→61 global skills, 19.2k→6.4k tok/session. Plugins beat local copies. →Tier A skill-bloat-and-promotion\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- **Portfolio dashboard** LIVE; `/project` re-renders+republishes. →Tier A command-centre, portfolio-registry-write-provenance.\\n- **Terminal (9/4)**: tmux = default VS Code shell; `cc`/`cx` aliases. →vault `Knowledge/tooling/tmux-cheat-sheet.md`.\\n- Hooks exist in TWO copies (`.claude/hooks/`, `.codex/hooks/`) — patch both. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo (`erash11/DEV`), 8 router `.md` only; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. `_ARCHIVE/` = parked. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Schedules/gws limits →automation-cadence. CFB capture (Mon, 8/24–1/23) →cfb-forecast-capture.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- **DUE (was 8/31)**: OKR Q1 gate: AI integration (buy-in) + data governance (Anthony's proposal).\\n- **Kitman vs MyLink**: MyLink intros (~half Kitman's cost) + buy Kitman API access. Undecided; blocks priority 3.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (5670 chars, updated 2026-09-12 13:35)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":856},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a86f4dbe-f4d0-4d87-9016-7a6031765e13","timestamp":"2026-09-13T04:30:28.611Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"d290860c-34be-4b50-ac6a-051bd16fb6c5","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"session-start-progressive-disclosure"}
{"parentUuid":"a86f4dbe-f4d0-4d87-9016-7a6031765e13","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"0f0e2f8d-d651-4ec1-abd6-8e7584892f0f","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nSaturday, September 12, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n260 compiled articles (195 concepts, 64 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n### Session (17:31)\\n\\n**Context:** Continuing the multi-task \\\"harness-agnostic AIOS\\\" plan (`~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`, pushed as `00730b6`) \\u2014 making the skills/backup stack work on both Mac and Windows. Tasks 1\\u20132 complete; paused, then resumed at round 10 of plan review.\\n\\n**Key Exchanges:**\\n- Codex hit its usage limit mid-gate (reset 4:46 PM). User said \\\"use claude, that fine\\\" \\u2192 reviewer switched to Claude via `--host codex`, which starts a fresh review session (resume can't cross providers).\\n- The Claude reviewer found what Codex missed: **14 of 19** outward symlinks in the skills repo are third-party package-manager installs (including 5 `mattpocock-skills` explicitly out of scope). Task 4 would have copied all of them into Eric's personal repo.\\n- Reframed the inventory: **42 skills Eric wrote, 19 third-party links.**\\n- Round-10 review findings (plan not yet approved): (1) serious \\u2014 the new safety hook silently breaks the daily backup: a refused commit is ignored but still logged as \\\"committed\\\", and the blocked link stays staged so every later backup fails silently; (2) minor \\u2014 text still says `.gitignore` where it should say `.git/info/exclude`; (3) minor \\u2014 the Pi test user may inherit the `staff` group, stalling that boundary step.\\n- User said \\\"pause\\\" (during an API ENOTFOUND error), then \\\"resume\\\".\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- Third-party vendored symlinks (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review`) stay **out** of the `claude-skills` repo \\u2014 same rule as plugins. Windows needs a separate install of that package. They were already committed and pushed as dead links on Windows; now explicit rather than silent.\\n- Task 4's inversion script deleted entirely \\u2014 leave the 19 third-party links alone rather than copy them in.\\n- Task 2 prune executed as a **move, not delete** (reversible).\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- **`.gitignore` patterns ending in `/` match directories but NOT symlinks** \\u2014 the trailing slash would have silently re-added all four dead links on the next backup run.\\n- Backups must be verified by **actually restoring them** \\u2014 the restore returned 57/61 skills, exposing a two-hop symlink chain (`~/.claude/skills/X \\u2192 ~/.agents/skills/X \\u2192 ~/.agents/vendor-review/...`) into an unbacked-up vendor folder.\\n- Re-run the review gate after amending a plan \\u2014 the prior approval is stale. Codex found 5 new bugs in the amendment itself.\\n- `dcg` blocks `mv` with variable paths; Python with explicit containment checks is the workaround.\\n- Directory counts can mismatch because `ls` omits hidden files (209 vs 208 was a hidden `.gitignore`).\\n- A second reviewer with a different provider catches different classes of error \\u2014 the provider switch wasn't just a fallback, it found the plan's biggest error.\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Fix the three round-10 findings: make the backup report a failed commit, have the sync unstage third-party links, correct `.gitignore` \\u2192 `.git/info/exclude` wording, handle the `staff`-group inheritance in the Pi boundary step.\\n- Re-run the review gate, then start Tasks 3\\u20138.\\n- Windows: separately install the vendored package that provides `claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review` (currently dead symlinks there).\\n- Task 2 result to record: global skills pool pruned 306 \\u2192 208; 61 skills still resolve; ~150 third-party installs untouched.\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":864},"type":"attachment","uuid":"71eae36b-a991-4e3a-81d4-62b492f14f25","timestamp":"2026-09-13T04:30:28.612Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"d290860c-34be-4b50-ac6a-051bd16fb6c5","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"session-start-progressive-disclosure"}
