{"parentUuid":"a93ad523-0ff7-4189-8a7a-65e088f86a5d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezoxEJi9MowFyzgW7KTv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Context:** Ran `/backup` (manual catch-up path for the KeystoneOS daily backup).\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- First run failed; second run succeeded after a fix. Final state: `status: OK`, 0 errors, `okCount: 80` (full count — SSD capture included).\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Renamed rather than deleted the stale SSD artifact: `/Volumes/CRASHBOX/AssistantBackup/DEV-nonrepo/LibraryProject/ZoteroInjestion/.git.stale-dir-2026-09-12` (139 MB). Reversible; safe to delete later since GitHub has the repo.\n- Archived a copy of `.errors.log`, then emptied it so the session-start HOOK FAILURE warning stops.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- **Submodule conversion breaks rsync backups.** On 9/11 `ZoteroInjestion` became a submodule inside `LibraryProject`, so its `.git` changed from a directory to a file. rsync cannot overwrite an existing destination directory with a file, so every backup failed while CRASHBOX was mounted. Fix = remove/rename the stale `.git` directory on the SSD.\n- A backup failure of this class only appears when the SSD is plugged in — it is invisible on SSD-absent runs.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Backup manifest still classifies `LibraryProject` as non-repo (`DEV-nonrepo/`); it now is a git repo with a GitHub remote. Backups work either way — Eric was asked whether to correct the entry; answer pending.\n- Optional cleanup: delete `.git.stale-dir-2026-09-12` on CRASHBOX whenever convenient."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42469,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":585,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_t